// A promissory note from Elena Brooks to Marcus Dunn (note.md).
Document "note.md"

Fact lender Identified by Marcus
Fact borrower Identified by Elena
Fact usd Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Fact instalment Identified by 1..12
Param loan : Money(USD, 2) = 1000000
Param regular : Money(USD, 2) = 86066
Param period : Duration = 30
Param grace : Duration = 10
Param default-after : Duration = 30

// 1. The loan
Bool lent
Var principal Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Act lend Actor lender Recipient borrower
  Holds when Not(lent())
  Creates lent(), principal(loan), interest(0), charged(0), paid(0), fees-paid(0)

// 2. Interest: a twelfth of six percent of the unpaid principal for every thirty days gone by
Fact fallen-due Identified by instalment
  Holds when Held(lent()) For period * instalment
Var interest Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Var charged Identified by Int
Fact interest-owing Identified by Money(USD, 2)
  Derived from interest-owing(interest + MulDivRound(principal, 6, 1200, NearestEven)
                 * (Count(Foreach instalment: instalment When fallen-due(instalment)) - charged))

// 3. Instalments, and 6.1: money paid ahead counts toward the next ones
Var paid Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Fact covered Identified by instalment
  Holds when instalment < 12 && paid >= regular * instalment
  Holds when principal == 0
Duty instalment-due Holder borrower Claimant lender Related to instalment
  Holds when fallen-due() && Not(covered())
  Violated when Held(lent()) For period * instalment + grace

// 4. Late fee: five percent of a regular instalment for each late instalment
Fact late Identified by instalment
  Holds when Violated(instalment-due())
Var fees-paid Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Fact fees-owing Identified by Money(USD, 2)
  Derived from fees-owing(MulDivRound(regular, 5, 100, NearestEven)
                 * Count(Foreach instalment: instalment When late(instalment)) - fees-paid)
Fact owing Identified by Money(USD, 2)
  Derived from owing(fees-owing + interest-owing + principal)

// 5 and 6. Payment, at any time, applied to fees, then interest, then principal
Act pay Actor borrower Recipient lender Related to usd
  Holds when lent() && usd <= owing
  Creates paid(paid + usd)
        , charged(Count(Foreach instalment: instalment When fallen-due(instalment)))
        , (Foreach instalment: late(instalment) When Violated(instalment-due()))
        , fees-paid(fees-paid + usd)                   When usd <= fees-owing
        , fees-paid(fees-paid + fees-owing)            When usd >  fees-owing
        , interest(interest-owing)                     When usd <= fees-owing
        , interest(fees-owing + interest-owing - usd)  When usd >  fees-owing && usd <= fees-owing + interest-owing
        , interest(0)                                  When usd >  fees-owing + interest-owing
        , principal(owing - usd)                       When usd >  fees-owing + interest-owing
Act charge-for-early-payment Actor lender Recipient borrower Holds when False

// 7. Default: thirty days unpaid, then the lender may call in everything
Bool called-in
Power call-in Actor lender Recipient borrower
  Holds when True
  Valid when (Exists instalment: instalment-due() && Held(lent()) For period * instalment + default-after)
  Creates called-in()
Duty everything-due Holder borrower Claimant lender
  Holds when called-in() && owing > 0
  Violated when True

Clause 1.1 Approved "97c6ec77d92784b06a5c8498785da9175f8cea5e21ea608e080e3d67cac50f51"
  Norm "Marcus Dunn, the lender, lends ten thousand dollars to Elena Brooks, the borrower, who promises to repay it with interest as this note says." => lend, pay
Clause 2.1 Approved "59b3cf60cde3fd86e275b935bd5961b2ebfb4ffaa4cfeec97e41eee59b4d289b"
  Definition "The unpaid principal bears simple interest at six percent a year. At the end of every thirty days after the loan is made, one twelfth of a year's interest on the principal then unpaid is added to the interest owing. Unpaid interest does not itself bear interest."
Clause 3.1 Approved "18bb909c47418e64c507deb53013e5da7fc828d85c2db2ec5897aad103669259"
  Norm "The borrower pays twelve instalments of eight hundred sixty dollars and sixty-six cents. The first falls due thirty days after the loan is made, and each of the others thirty days after the one before." => instalment-due, pay
Clause 3.2 Approved "91a83855b4a6d44af68dc0baaf124253c09ee22815316a6970ae8a7c96cfa2cb"
  Norm "The twelfth instalment is whatever is then owing, whether that is more or less than the others." => instalment-due
Clause 4.1 Approved "d5e126a8e0afd6e3978235e8e34712c691dc6eb534ebe16b189035aded5e3205"
  Norm "An instalment that is not paid in full within ten days after it falls due is late." => instalment-due
  Definition " For each late instalment the borrower owes a late fee of five percent of a regular instalment."
Clause 5.1 Approved "30ca8c6548073cec6b872056d30c99b177d9cae947694e3d30546e25fd961fd8"
  Norm "Every payment is applied first to late fees, then to interest, and then to principal." => pay
Clause 6.1 Approved "6355e48fad6196517852a37f2a8ba500fb23432151bf6f1c2312d87e79b27c6a"
  Norm "The borrower may pay all or part of what is owing ahead of time." => pay
  Norm " The lender charges nothing for early payment." => charge-for-early-payment
  Norm " Money paid ahead of time counts toward the instalments that fall due next." => instalment-due
Clause 7.1 Approved "0316c45a37510d8b59aad968c5fc3ababf93b0b609ac852bf6715891620a1fd8"
  Norm "If an instalment is still unpaid thirty days after it falls due, the lender may, by notice to the borrower, declare everything owing due at once." => call-in, everything-due
  Norm " A notice given before then has no effect." => call-in
.
